# Response headers, honoured by Cloudflare Pages.
#
# GitHub Pages could not send these: `actions/deploy-pages` uploads files and
# Pages answers them with a fixed header set, with no per-repository way to add
# one. Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the deployed directory
# instead, which is why it lives in `public/` — the Angular assets glob copies it
# verbatim into `dist/deepwork-site/browser`, and Pages parses it there rather
# than serving it.
#
# The syntax is Cloudflare's, not Apache's: a URL pattern on its own line, then
# indented `Name: value` pairs. Rules are applied in file order, and a header set
# twice is joined with a comma — which is why the `/contact*` block below *detaches*
# the policy in force before setting its own. Two Content-Security-Policy headers
# would both be enforced, and the intersection of the two would block hCaptcha.
#
# Every host in the policies below is one the site actually loads, not a guess:
#   'self'                        the bundle, fonts, screenshots, favicons
#   googletagmanager.com          the disclosed Google tag (src/index.html)
#   google-analytics.com          the GA4 property that tag configures
#   analytics.google.com          GA4's regional collection endpoint
#   www.google.com                where GA4 actually posts `g/collect`; found by
#                                 loading the built page under this policy and
#                                 reading the one violation it produced
#   pagead2.googlesyndication.com the AdSense script on the page and the guides
#   *.googlesyndication.com       the ad frames and the resources they fetch
#   *.doubleclick.net             ad delivery, measurement and frequency capping
#   *.googleadservices.com        the ad-click path
#   adservice.google.com          the ad-serving endpoint
#   www.googletagservices.com     Google's ad-tag loader
#   *.adtrafficquality.google     Google's invalid-traffic checks for the ads
#   *.gstatic.com                 static resources the ad frames request
#   fundingchoicesmessages.google.com
#                                 the consent message Google serves in the
#                                 EEA, UK and Switzerland
#   deepwork.goatcounter.com      the first-party pageview (src/app/core/analytics.ts)
#   web3forms.com                 the contact form's script and endpoint
#   hcaptcha.com / hcaptcha.net   the captcha the form requires
#
# `'unsafe-inline'` in script-src is not laziness: Tag Manager injects inline
# script by design, and the theme is applied by an inline script before first
# paint. A nonce would have to be threaded through both, and GTM's injected
# containers would still need it. What is left is still worth having —
# frame-ancestors, base-uri, form-action, object-src and a closed connect-src are
# the directives that matter on a page with no user-supplied content.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://www.googletagservices.com https://adservice.google.com https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://adservice.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://*.gstatic.com https://www.google.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.google.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://adservice.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.adtrafficquality.google https://*.gstatic.com https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://deepwork.goatcounter.com; frame-src https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://tpc.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.googleadservices.com https://fundingchoicesmessages.google.com https://www.google.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'

# The contact form is the one page with a third party whose own documentation
# requires allowances: hCaptcha asks for `script-src` and `frame-src` to include
# hcaptcha.com and *.hcaptcha.com, and the widget answers on connect-src too.
# The policy is detached and re-set rather than extended, for the reason in the
# header comment. `worker-src blob:` and `child-src blob:` are for the challenge
# step, which runs its proof of work in a worker created from a blob URL.
# The selector is `/contact*` rather than `/contact/*` on purpose: it matches
# `/contact`, `/contact/` and `/contact/index.html` without depending on whether a
# splat is allowed to match an empty remainder.
/contact*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://web3forms.com https://hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.net; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com https://web3forms.com https://hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.net; frame-src https://hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.com https://*.hcaptcha.net; child-src blob:; worker-src 'self' blob:
